                                                                  9137 1451
 FILE ASSEMBLY, VERIFICATION AND VALIDATION                       9137 1451
 A. Trkov, IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                  9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 The ENDF-formatted data from EMPIRE calculation were merged      9137 1451
 consistently with the resonance data (see description below).    9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 No delayed neutron data are available in any evaluated data      9137 1451
 library. Average number of delayed neutrons and delayed neutron  9137 1451
 spectra were assumed to be the same as for Pa-231, taken from    9137 1451
 JENDL-3.3 and extrapolated flat to 60 MeV.                       9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 The assembled file was checked according to the IAEA             9137 1451
 verification procedure [1]. None of the checking codes reported  9137 1451
 any significant warnings. Comparison with experimental data      9137 1451
 from EXFOR confirmed that the data are representative of the     9137 1451
 database on which the evaluation is based. The ACE file for      9137 1451
 Monte Carlo transport calculations was produced as a result of   9137 1451
 the checking process, including standard plots. No specific      9137 1451
 benchmarks sensitive to Pa-233 data were identified, therefore   9137 1451
 further validation could not be performed. Plots and other       9137 1451
 details are available on the above-defined web page of the CRP.  9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 [1] A. Trkov: Guidelines for Nuclear Data Verification and       9137 1451
     Validation, International Atomic Energy Agency, Vienna,      9137 1451
     Austria, INDC(SEC)-0107, August 2005.                        9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
  ***************************************************             9137 1451
 FAST ENERGY REGION                                               9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 Authors:                                                         9137 1451
 Roberto Capote (IAEA/NAPC, Nuclear Data Section)                 9137 1451
 Mihaela Sin (University of Bucharest, Romania)                   9137 1451
 Andrej Trkov (IAEA/NAPC, Nuclear Data Section)                   9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 EVALUATION PROCEDURE                                             9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                9137 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               9137 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              9137 1451
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-2.19b33 by                    9137 1451
 M. Herman et al [He01, He02]. This code integrates               9137 1451
 into a single system a number of important modules               9137 1451
 and features, relevant for this evaluation:                      9137 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 9137 1451
   coupled-channels (ECIS03 by J. Raynal)                         9137 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    9137 1451
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              9137 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      9137 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 9137 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                9137 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   9137 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                9137 1451
   discrete transitions                                           9137 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL-2 library [Ri03]              9137 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                9137 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               9137 1451
   and gamma strength functions  based on the RIPL-2              9137 1451
   library [Ri03]                                                 9137 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              9137 1451
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           9137 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    9137 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 9137 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                9137 1451
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      9137 1451
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        9137 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 9137 1451
 current evaluation:                                              9137 1451
                                                                  9137 1451
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-2 level                 9137 1451
 file, based on the 1998 version of ENSDF.                        9137 1451
 Prompt fission neutron spectra and nubar                         9137 1451
 calculation include contributions from Pa and Th chains          9137 1451
 (see description of the method in Maslov V.M. et al,             9137 1451
 Eur.Phys.J.A18(2003)93). Nubar evaluation is based               9137 1451
 on calculations carried out by A. Tudora, G. Vladuca             9137 1451
 and F.-J.Hambsch below the first fission chance. Above           9137 1451
 that both post-fission and pre-fission neutrons were             9137 1451
 considered. Prefission neutrons angular distribution             9137 1451
 assumed anisotropic following (n,xn) distribution.               9137 1451
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  9137 1451
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  3             9137 1451
 Width fluctuations calculated within HRTW  up to 0.30 MeV        9137 1451
 Coupled Channels (ECIS) used for direct inelastic scattering     9137 1451
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      9137 1451
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            9137 1451
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           9137 1451
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS set to  1.7                   9137 1451
 Max hole number in PCROSS set to 0.20*sqrt(g*U)                  9137 1451
    being U the CN excitation energy                              9137 1451
 For all nuclei: advanced treatment of fission                    9137 1451
 Emission width of ejectile 0 from 234Pa multiplied by   4.900    9137 1451
 E1 strength function set to MLO1                                 9137 1451
 GDR parameters from RIPL-2/Exp.data+Plujko systematics           9137 1451
